1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,420
Hello there!

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:02,820
Hello there!

3
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,040
Hello there!

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,940
We're losing our dungeon?

5
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,340
So much for guard duty.

6
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,880
That maniac fused the
Stratum Lords together.

7
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:32,554
I'm guessing they're on their
way to the fortified city.

8
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:35,417
Fly if you have wings, and
run if you're fleet-footed!

9
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,197
Tell the Empire and nearby towns
and villages what's coming?

10
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,440
You got it!

11
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,457
We intend to follow them,
but what about your group?

12
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,437
You can count on us to take
down some monster scum.

13
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:50,520
Least we can do to pay Boxo
back for his sacrifice!

14
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,750
Yes.

15
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:54,187
We'll gladly risk our
lives to aid the cause.

16
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:55,695
We've got to do this.

17
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,797
Otherwise, we forfeit our man cards.

18
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,457
You in, bro? You know it.

19
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,437
I'll do anything.

20
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,873
I can't let a box be more manly than me.

21
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:04,317
We must buy some time.

22
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,940
For the sake of Boxo.

23
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:07,945
I'd like to stay by your side.

24
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,786
I'm aware I can't atone
for my prior villainy.

25
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:12,620
I'll go with you.

26
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:16,517
Personally speaking, I don't think
I'll ever truly forgive them.

27
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:20,517
I'll stay behind and help dig
up Boxo. Pity, too. I'll...

28
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,857
I'll help...

29
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:23,000
from here.

30
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:24,480
I'm staying put.

31
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:27,857
Will want to use my magic
items to help with the digging.

32
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:31,917
Nothing would please me more than to
help rescue our valiant master, Boxxo.

33
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,177
Alas, I'm certain if I don't turn
my blade to slaying monsters,

34
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:36,397
he'll be angry with me.

35
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,715
So I tearfully trust this task to you.

36
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,500
That leaves Lamas.

37
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:42,760
But I don't even need to ask.

38
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:55,660
The whole thing is unbearable.

39
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:59,392
But every last one of us knows
he's still alive out there.

40
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:10,360
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box.

41
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,797
But inside, I've still got a human soul.

42
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,277
In this new world of wonders,

43
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:17,857
I travel to and fro on the back of
my super strong partner, Llamas.

44
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:19,940
The name's Boxxo. Hello there.

45
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,868
That means yes, by the way!

46
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,110
했

47
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,380
Yeah

48
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:09,560
Yeah Yeah Yeah Yeah

49
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,197
We've already overtaken
the monster's army.

50
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:41,280
The Akar's speed never ceases to amaze me.

51
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:42,870
Indeed.

52
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:45,257
And it's a good omen that
it hasn't disappeared.

53
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:49,458
That would seem to suggest that our
friend Boxo is still in one piece.

54
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:50,876
What of the surface?

55
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,040
I hope my sister is unharmed.

56
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,352
We're really hauling it.

57
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:57,677
Won't take long to reach
the fortified city.

58
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,940
Maybe a week tops?

59
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:03,462
But since we can't risk entering
the aptly named Murderous Forest,

60
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,450
we'll have to go around.

61
00:04:04,533 --> 00:04:05,363
Meanwhile,

62
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:10,306
our foes will undoubtedly cut through,
with that enormous beast leading the way.

63
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:11,290
I know.

64
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:15,097
I'll charge into the murderous
forest and keep the dastards busy.

65
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:17,709
With luck, that'll buy
us the time we need.

66
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,861
That kind of idea's a death wish.

67
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,677
Are you so eager to lose your life?

68
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,480
No, I'll never die.

69
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,420
It would displease
Master Boxo if I did so.

70
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:30,011
I guess there's no getting through to him.

71
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,457
Swear to me on Boxo's honor.

72
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,377
That you'll return to our ranks.

73
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,157
Still alive and kicking.

74
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,070
I swear.

75
00:04:37,153 --> 00:04:39,097
And you better get to it!

76
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:42,117
Remember to value your
life above all else.

77
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,757
I second the motion.

78
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:45,977
Living is vastly preferable to dying.

79
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,597
Cherish your life along with your boots.

80
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,820
I shall.

81
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,837
Try not to die.

82
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,220
If things get hairy, make a run for it.

83
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:15,700
Only cowards lurk in the shadows.

84
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:20,700
I find it exhilarating that
you can sense my presence.

85
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,240
Who are you?

86
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:23,900
Good question.

87
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:27,557
I don't recall what my name was
before I was a bag of bones.

88
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:31,640
It doesn't matter anymore, as I now
answer to four-fingered general.

89
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:35,137
I didn't expect to find one
of the five-finger generals.

90
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,140
I'm curious.

91
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,697
They say only a master
swordsman could have cut

92
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,957
through the bars of the
Pinky General's cell.

93
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,511
Are you the one to blame?

94
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,010
Guilty.

95
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:47,061
I was called in to clean
up the mess she had made.

96
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,860
Oh, what joy! What bliss!

97
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:54,477
It's been an eternity since
someone blocked by opening strike.

98
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,440
This should be quite amusing.

99
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,297
We're running the right way, right?

100
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:03,210
Right.

101
00:06:03,293 --> 00:06:04,123
Just keep running.

102
00:06:04,206 --> 00:06:06,497
The map said the next town's at
the foot of that little mountain,

103
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,817
so that's where we're going.

104
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:10,960
We'd better hurry. Oh, wow. Drill-worthy.

105
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:13,217
The village and the veggies are abandoned.

106
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:17,537
I'm not even a salad gal, but those greens
are calling my name and I'm listening.

107
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:21,497
Who would have thought something could
smell healthy and yummy at the same time?

108
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,077
Can we stuff our faces now?

109
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:25,377
Yeah, but let's try not to eat at all.

110
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:27,754
I bet other animals want in on it, too.

111
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,100
Well, let's dive in!

112
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:31,540
It's eat a claw!

113
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,150
Ahh!

114
00:06:33,233 --> 00:06:34,140
A new experience!

115
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:37,417
It's all juicy and splashes
around in my mouth when I bite it!

116
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,088
Plus it has a rich
flavor losing with umami!

117
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,077
I don't believe it!

118
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:41,990
I can't!

119
00:06:42,073 --> 00:06:44,377
I need to know what they could
eat a veggie like thinker!

120
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:47,717
Imagine combining these veggies
with the whole lot of fried chicken!

121
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,717
I like these veggies even better
than the ones from Kikuyu.

122
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,937
Though they kind of remind me of
her stock when I think about it.

123
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,491
Wonder what that's about.

124
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:03,120
He's good.

125
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,441
I doubt I'll be able to best him.

126
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,760
But I must.

127
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:09,077
I cannot allow this enemy to roam free.

128
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:12,217
Lest the friends I left behind
pay dearly for my failure.

129
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,418
I must end this battle here and now.

130
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:15,490
Interesting.

131
00:07:15,573 --> 00:07:17,597
You're aware my skills surpass your own.

132
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,327
Yet you refuse to back down.

133
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,755
I have my reasons for standing strong.

134
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,440
Well, how fortuitous.

135
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:27,541
I had grown weary of cutting down
opponents as they flee in terror.

136
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,140
Forgive me, Master Boxo.

137
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:32,560
It seems I'm destined to
meet my end here. And yet,

138
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,920
even as my life slips away from me,

139
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:38,276
I swear to give this final
battle everything I've got!

140
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:49,020
Well now, a commendable last-ditch effort.

141
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:51,640
I accept this fascinating challenge.

142
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,020
An Essex?

143
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,350
Unbelievable.

144
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:06,060
Usaka! Usarion! Usarion! Usabi!

145
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:08,637
Keep our enemy distracted
as long as you can!

146
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,977
Good sir, please hurry!

147
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,817
Now's your chance to make a run for it!

148
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,730
Hayachi?

149
00:08:12,813 --> 00:08:14,268
Mishwa, is that really you?

150
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,696
We'll have to exchange stories later.

151
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:20,637
For the time being, our top
priority is defeating this guy.

152
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,550
Agreed.

153
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,177
If you're open to suggestions,

154
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:26,337
may I ask that you instruct the
Essex to continue distracting him?

155
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,800
As you wish. Hey, Usata!

156
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:31,041
Keep whittling away at the enemy!

157
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,260
Truly a valiant effort, Mishuel!

158
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,337
You've come so far.

159
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:59,377
In truth, I would have been
doomed were it not for the Essex.

160
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:01,497
Did you hear that, my furry friends?

161
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:03,597
Allow me to introduce you, Mishuel.

162
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,020
This is Usata, the head of the family.

163
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:10,337
The elegant damsel next to him with
the beautiful fluffy coat is Usarion.

164
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:14,580
And the tiny versions of them are
their children, Usarion and Usapi.

165
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:18,537
How is it that I had no idea you
were an animal trainer, sister?

166
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,267
And they're rather powerful.

167
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,049
I'm not an animal trainer.

168
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,617
These little fuzzballs
are my friends and allies.

169
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,530
I see.

170
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,117
By the way, what are you doing
in such a dangerous place?

171
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,847
I could ask the same of you.

172
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:34,079
You are the eighth princess
of this land, after all.

173
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:38,525
As there is much to share, I
suggest an exchange of information.

174
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:58,880
Rest, Lamas.

175
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,937
You've been working yourself to the bone.

176
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:04,117
You can't help Boxxo if you
keel over dead from exhaustion.

177
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,030
She's right.

178
00:10:05,113 --> 00:10:07,457
You know Boxxo would be mad
if he could see you like this.

179
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,370
Rest!

180
00:10:08,453 --> 00:10:10,500
When Bokso's buried in the dirt!

181
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:16,300
I understand.

182
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,217
That all makes complete sense.

183
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:19,130
As for me,

184
00:10:19,213 --> 00:10:20,597
I came from the fortified city when we

185
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:23,157
caught wind something
was amiss in the forest.

186
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,177
The matter of the Guardian
had only just been

187
00:10:25,260 --> 00:10:28,137
settled when the dungeon
met with that untimely fate.

188
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,050
The Guardian?

189
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,860
Of the fortified city.

190
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:34,668
He left us to fight the Demon
Lord, but he was badly injured.

191
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:37,057
It was only recently that we
learned of his whereabouts.

192
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,597
He was able to recover just the other day.

193
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,757
I didn't know such a person existed.

194
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,637
I've been in the dungeon a good while,

195
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:46,537
so forgive me for being
behind on current events.

196
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,450
Mishuel,

197
00:10:47,533 --> 00:10:50,997
it's been a long time since I heard any
news about you and I've been worried sick.

198
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:53,560
That whole time, you were in the dungeon?

199
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,232
Tell me everything about your new master.

200
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:57,502
Where to start?

201
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,994
His heart is most sincere and generous.

202
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:03,817
He keeps a calm demeanor no matter
how treacherous the situation.

203
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,737
He protects and cares for his friends.

204
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:10,800
The Guardian sounds extremely commendable,
but Master Boxo is utterly magnificent.

205
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,459
Still your tongue!

206
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:14,597
Though I'll admit Boxo
sounds extraordinary,

207
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:18,157
you would be remiss to suggest that he
could possibly surpass the Guardian.

208
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,040
I must beg your pardon.

209
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,640
It wasn't my intention to
belittle him, I swear. Still,

210
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,297
the truth remains that
there isn't a person

211
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:27,497
in the world who holds
a candle to Master Boxo.

212
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:28,410
Not so fast!

213
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,837
The Guardian is most
generous and open-minded.

214
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,377
Truly a being without evil.

215
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:35,754
Actually, you don't know what
Master Boxo is capable of.

216
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:43,237
Perhaps we should save this lively
debate for when our work is finished.

217
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,150
Agreed.

218
00:11:44,233 --> 00:11:46,637
If we're unable to slow down
the monster army here and now,

219
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:49,779
I fear the fortified city
will very soon be overrun.

220
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:53,997
With your friends notifying the city
dwellers, there's no cause for concern.

221
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:56,677
But just to be safe, I'll
help you set some traps.

222
00:11:56,760 --> 00:12:00,037
With Usata and the others here,
we can even process timber.

223
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,597
I'll make you proud, Master.

224
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:02,510
You'll see.

225
00:12:02,593 --> 00:12:04,637
I'll distract the fiends without delay and

226
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,367
buy enough time for you
to join us in battle!

227
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:15,944
It appears we'll reach the fortified
city sooner than we thought.

228
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:19,766
Also, I wasn't expecting to behold
such abundant farmland here.

229
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,772
The city has recently become
renowned for its agriculture.

230
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:28,611
I hear the impeccable quality of their
vegetables is the talk of the Empire.

231
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:32,114
The city's lord must be a
rather shrewd business person.

232
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:35,737
Is there anything useful you can
tell us about them, Director?

233
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,100
Of course there is.

234
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:41,637
They say she's beautiful and succeeded
her father at a young age a few years ago.

235
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,797
Oh, and also, this one's important.

236
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,920
It's best to avoid eye contact.

237
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:49,120
I hear it's especially
risky for human males.

238
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,400
Don't be ridiculous.

239
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:56,077
You make it sound like we'll fall in
love the moment we lock eyes with her.

240
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,380
Your wait is over.

241
00:12:57,780 --> 00:13:00,074
The lady has arrived and we'll see you.

242
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,080
I'm sorry for keeping you waiting.

243
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:13,797
My name is Jessica.

244
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:16,527
and as the ruling lady,
I welcome all of you.

245
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:18,980
I think we finally met our match.

246
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:20,417
I already have a girlfriend.

247
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:23,297
I can't remember her name,
but I know she exists.

248
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:42,477
Pull it together. I have.

249
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,140
Those shoes were orgasmic.

250
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:48,357
My feelings for Lady Jessica have
reached their climax and been expelled.

251
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,677
Please, young master...

252
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,200
Please, m 'lady.

253
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:54,497
It's important that you stop spreading
your charm so indiscriminately,

254
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:56,460
as it's causing problems again.

255
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:58,897
I completely agree with Master Stuck.

256
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:01,477
Those eyes can turn
honest men into horndogs,

257
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:04,501
so it's best for everyone
if you keep them closed.

258
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,737
I see.

259
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:10,217
So we're dealing with the
forces of the Netherlord,

260
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,697
or rather the Left-Armed General.

261
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:15,000
despite our negotiations
with the Demon Lord's forces.

262
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:19,007
I beg your pardon, but what
negotiations are you referring to?

263
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,737
Currently, we're trying
to negotiate an armistice.

264
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:24,577
We've been working on it
with the Demon Lord's forces.

265
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:27,719
It seemed like we were
making considerable progress.

266
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:28,770
Lady Jessica,

267
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,237
the Left-Armed General has earned quite
the reputation as a no-good schemer.

268
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:35,496
Meaning he was trying to seize power.

269
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,420
My dear Steck,

270
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:40,157
please send a messenger to
the Demon Lord's territory and

271
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,677
let us hope the Guardian returns
before the enemy reaches us.

272
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:46,897
Motor, explain the situation
to our soldiers and citizens.

273
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:49,577
If that is what you wish,
then consider it done.

274
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:51,366
I'll take care of everything.

275
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:55,086
You must be exhausted
after your long journey.

276
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,122
Give me just a moment to
arrange lodging for you.

277
00:14:58,580 --> 00:14:59,521
In the meantime,

278
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:03,417
please help yourself to some fresh
vegetables harvested from our land.

279
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,717
Those are the tastiest looking
vegetables I've ever seen!

280
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:07,630
I know.

281
00:15:07,713 --> 00:15:09,137
I'm literally drooling like an animal.

282
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:13,240
Such a delightful feast is worthy
of my full attention. True.

283
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,280
It's life-changing!

284
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,899
That's the ticket.

285
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:22,997
We'll just keep on whittling
him down from the rear.

286
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:24,300
I'll use my magic.

287
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:25,540
I'll join you.

288
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,152
She mixed magic with her daughter-in-law.

289
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,480
That was brutal.

290
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,682
What are you jabbering on about?

291
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,877
He called me his daughter-in-law?

292
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:41,200
Um, Big Sasori? Yes,
Kai? What's the matter?

293
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,915
Don't worry about it.

294
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,692
This world is too cruel!

295
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:47,077
Kai stole all the Lady
Killer genes from himself!

296
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:47,990
He really did!

297
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:48,930
But it's okay.

298
00:15:49,013 --> 00:15:52,177
When Boxo's back, we'll guilt him
into teaching us how to up our game!

299
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:54,142
Now you're speaking my language!

300
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:58,677
I hope they're already digging
him out and dusting him off.

301
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,407
We owe the big luck big
time for what he did.

302
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:02,740
Most certainly.

303
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:05,940
And it's high time we paid back our debt.

304
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:10,313
Let's start by mopping up some monsters.

305
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,205
We've got your back over here.

306
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,877
Let's show them how it's done.

307
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:17,019
Our hungry little spears
will dine on monster blood.

308
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,860
The star attraction has arrived.

309
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:24,060
You trainers are in for
a special treat today.

310
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:28,140
I'm sure you're already aware
I'm the shouting songstress.

311
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:32,817
In other words, the terrifying and
titillating pinky General Kyle rings.

312
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:37,540
And I'm here to make sure every
one of you suffers and dies.

313
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:41,722
I'm told you were captured
but managed to escape.

314
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:44,977
Sulream, it feels like it's been forever.

315
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:48,437
But I never liked you
anyway, so no harm, no foul.

316
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:52,837
Now I have the pleasure of personally
killing the Ringfinger General.

317
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:56,400
I must admit, it's a dream, Control.

318
00:17:13,940 --> 00:17:16,060
I think the corpses are combining.

319
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,180
That's nasty.

320
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:18,880
This is quite absurd.

321
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:21,577
Can someone please
explain what's happening?

322
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,680
She's a necromancer, and
she's in her element.

323
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:27,157
As you can see,

324
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:31,397
a delicious assortment of monsters and
humans were tragically buried alive.

325
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:34,160
I'm swallowed by a nasty landslide!

326
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,840
Impressed yet?

327
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:44,260
I call this my army of rot stitched
together from fugitive corpses!

328
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:48,180
Because how freakin' metal is that?

329
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,180
How cute you came to play!

330
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:52,615
That makes this easy!

331
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,980
It means I don't have to hold back!

332
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,160
F you!

333
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:11,980
You see that?

334
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:14,417
I was able to resist your pathetic attack.

335
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,977
You're playing it cool, but it's an act!

336
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,397
Got the theatrics, babe.

337
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:22,539
Cause I know that last attempt must
have drained a crap ton of honor.

338
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:26,237
Now I finally get to jump
on that smug little face!

339
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,540
Let's make this chick bleed.

340
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,620
Now die!

341
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,540
This is no time to nap!

342
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:38,440
Keep going!

343
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:40,916
Why the hell are you plopping around?

344
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:45,160
Hey, what's the meaning of this?

345
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:51,820
Why are your arms and legs
turning to you? Forgive me.

346
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,265
I'm the one who's responsible.

347
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:55,520
That's not fair!

348
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,117
Since when does the kid have wings?

349
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,540
And how the hell did you decay my army?

350
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:05,097
When the dungeon master set about removing
my blessing of decay, I made a request.

351
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:09,077
I wished to be able to use it at
will instead of losing it completely.

352
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,757
You're talking out of your butt!

353
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:14,077
Though if you say you're the one
to blame, I'll have to kill you!

354
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,180
Is that right?

355
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,357
You think I'd let you kill my boy?

356
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:19,237
Now's as good a time as any to show off!

357
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:21,732
This crazy lady was just our opening act!

358
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:33,040
That's one obstacle
down, but it's not over.

359
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,280
She looks pretty miffed.

360
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:39,377
It's going to be hard to get her to
understand why I kept this from her.

361
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:42,377
If we're running low, I'll
chop some more wood for us.

362
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:45,437
If anyone's backing muscle,
come help me lift something.

363
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:48,397
I'll put whatever you want on
your tab, so eat your fill.

364
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,598
You're so generous.

365
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:51,397
Munami, you have work to do.

366
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:52,620
Are you happy?

367
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:56,037
It was worth it, even though it was
a risk bringing all that seasoning.

368
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:56,950
Yep!

369
00:19:57,033 --> 00:19:57,935
You're the best, Mom!

370
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:01,700
Miss Lori, we'll be
ready to depart shortly.

371
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,357
Let me know when we're good to go.

372
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,317
We'll leave as soon as
my things are loaded.

373
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:06,230
About that.

374
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:09,777
The monsters that emerge from the
dungeon might still be present.

375
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:13,437
That said, it's far too dangerous
to leave without a hunter escort.

376
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:16,637
We'll need every ounce of
manpower to rebuild this place,

377
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:19,017
which means we'll just
have to manage on our own.

378
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:23,980
And besides, I have the utmost faith in
everyone we've entrusted with our lives.

379
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:27,140
Though really,

380
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:31,812
this will undoubtedly be wasted effort
when Boxxo inevitably returns to us.

381
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:35,600
Ladies, I can't offer
any work for a spell.

382
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:39,212
So if you wish to profit, you
should move to another town.

383
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:42,440
Does this mean you're staying?

384
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:46,197
But the only pounding to do
here is with hammers and nails.

385
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:48,577
Miss Shirley, we still
owe you for taking us in.

386
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:50,637
We'll follow wherever you lead us.

387
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:53,955
I'm sure there isn't a better
boss in the entire world.

388
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,420
Such silliness.

389
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,040
But sure, I'll take it.

390
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:02,060
We'll rebuild, then resume our good
work draining lonely men of money.

391
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:20,880
That's our Llamas.

392
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:23,497
It's clear you'll never
change, no matter what.

393
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:24,657
He's still alive!

394
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:27,820
I gotta hurry and save him,
before he isn't anymore!

395
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:28,981
Save the speech.

396
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:33,257
You know I'm not gonna stop you from
searching, but I won't let you go overboard.

397
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:34,170
Okay.

398
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:35,470
See this?

399
00:21:35,553 --> 00:21:37,873
It's a magic item that probes for souls.

400
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,040
Does it dig?

401
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:45,067
It won't help with labor, but it's possible
it can help us locate Bokso's soul.

402
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,340
Hello there!

403
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:38,860
I love you.

404
00:23:14,020 --> 00:23:15,860
Let's go.

405
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:21,660
I'm waiting for you.

406
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:32,936
I'm waiting for you.
